    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-womens-health-engineering-and-digital-technologies/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies The School of Engineering at EPFL invites applications for a faculty position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies. Appointments will be at the Tenure Track Assistant Professor level. We seek exceptional individuals who will develop and lead a research program at the forefront of the discipline and who will have a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate-level teaching. We are seeking innovative researchers to advance engineering-driven solutions in women’s healthcare, focusing on personalized monitoring, diagnostics, and treatment. Relevant expertise includes wearable sensors, organoids, microfluidics, advanced imaging, biomedical microsystems, and AI-based analytics, with emphasis on data-driven approaches that integrate sex-specific physiology and enable clinically impactful, minimally invasive technologies across the lifespan. This endowed chair is supported by the Leister Foundation and the Institute for Women’s Health ( https://instituteforwomenshealth.org ), a Swiss non-profit initiative dedicated to supporting and translating patient-centred research into improved health outcomes for women. Thematic links to research topics at the Institute of Bioengineering, and wherever relevant at the School of Engineering, School of Life Sciences and School of Computer and Communication Sciences, are strongly encouraged. The candidate’s ability to teach STEM subjects and/or bioengineering topics will be a key selection criterion. EPFL offers world-class research infrastructures and core facilities. Its environment is multilingual and multicultural. Switzerland has an exceptionally high human development index and consistently ranks highly in quality of life, economic competitiveness, and innovation. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter, a curriculum vitae including a publication list, a synopsis of major accomplishments, and a concise statement of future research agenda and teaching interests, along with the names and contact information of three to five references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: October 1st, 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044486 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Carlotta Guiducci Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : [email protected] Further information about EPFL and our School is available at epfl.ch , sti.epfl.ch and bioengineering.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives 