    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-computational-modeling-in-chemistry-or-chemical-engineering/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering EPFL is a leading university with strong emphasis on basic sciences, engineering and life sciences. Research within its Institute of Chemical Sciences and Engineering (ISIC) includes synthetic, biological, physical, analytical, and theoretical chemistry as well as chemical engineering. ISIC is leading an international multi-domain effort to promote the development of energy- and environmentally sustainable separation processes via a National Centre of Competence in Research: NCCR Separations, composed of ~20 research groups at EPFL, ETHZ, Northwestern University, University of Alberta, and further Swiss Institutes and Universities: https://www.nccr-separations.ch We invite applications for a Tenure Track Assistant Professor in chemistry and chemical engineering with a strong link to computational modelling. Specific areas of interest include, but are not limited to, molecular simulations, electronic structure theory, thermodynamic modeling, machine-learning and artificial intelligence based methods, with applications broadly related to separation technologies. We seek candidates with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels and an outstanding research record. As professor of chemistry or chemical engineering, the successful candidate is expected to initiate and develop a creative research and teaching program at the forefront of the discipline. The candidate will actively participate in the NCCR Separations to accelerate the development of efficient separation processes, bridging fundamental insights to real-world impact. Significant start-up resources, research budget (including a fixed annual allocation for salaries and consumables) and state-of-the-art research infra­structure are available. Salaries and benefits are internationally competitive. We offer a highly international environment that is multi-lingual and multi-cultural. Applications must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, publications list, concise statements of research and teaching interests as well as the names and addresses (including email) of three to five references who are ready to supply a recommendation letter upon request. Application deadline: October 15th, 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044487 Enquiries regarding the position may be addressed to: Prof. Kumar Varoon Agrawal ; ( [email protected] ) Delegate Chair of the search committee Co-Director, NCCR Separations For additional information on EPFL and ISIC, please consult: epfl.ch or isic.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply . About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-experimantal-particle-physics/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics The School of Basic Sciences at EPFL invites applications for a faculty position in experimental particle physics . The appointment will be at the Tenure Track level, with an expected start date in 2027 (or mutually agreed upon). Applications from any sub-field of particle physics are welcome. Candidates with expertise in artificial intelligence and/or detector instrumentation are particularly encouraged to apply. The faculty position offers the opportunity to join the experimental high-energy physics group at the Institute of Physics (IPHYS) of EPFL. The group has been strongly involved in the LHCb experiment at CERN’s Large Hadron Collider since its inception and will contribute to the second detector upgrade, which will enable enhanced data-taking capabilities, extending the experiment’s scientific reach beyond 2036. The group is also engaged in the preparation of possible new experiments at the FCC-ee, recommended as the next CERN flagship collider. The position offers the opportunity to join the LHCb collaboration while developing ideas for the longer-term, in an environment providing strong technical support in detector development and the possibility to collaborate with theoreticians. Candidates should hold a PhD in particle physics or a closely related field and demonstrate an outstanding record of scientific achievement, innovation, and leadership commensurate with their career stage. The successful applicant is expected to develop a creative and ambitious experimental research programme, supervise students and researchers, attract external funding, and engage in physics teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels, with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching. EPFL, with its main campus located in Lausanne, Switzerland, on the shores of Lake Geneva, is a dynamically growing and well-funded institution fostering excellence and diversity. It has an international campus with world-class infrastructure, including high-performance computing. The EPFL environment is multi-lingual and multi-cultural, with English serving as a common interface. EPFL covers a wide spectrum of science and engineering and offers a fertile environment for research and cooperation between different disciplines. It has a wide international network as well as strong links with research institutions in Switzerland, in particular with CERN and the Paul Scherrer Institute. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter including a statement of motivation; curriculum vitae; publication list; research statement; statement of teaching interests; as well as the names and contact of three to five references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: 15 October 2026 Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044488 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Jean-Paul Kneib Director of the EPFL Institute of Physics Chair of the Search Committee E-mail: [email protected] Further information on EPFL, SB, and IPHYS is available at epfl.ch , sb.epfl.ch , and iphys.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-positions-in-finance/": {
      "title": "Faculty Positions in Finance ‒ Working",
      "description": "Faculty Positions in Finance ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL When you access EPFL websites, we may set cookies on your devices and process personal data about you in accordance with our privacy policy . You can block cookies by using your browser settings. OK Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Positions in Finance Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Positions in Finance The College of Management of Technology (CDM) at EPFL invites applications for two faculty positions in Finance . Appointments will be at the Tenure Track Assistant or (Tenured) Associate Professor level, with an expected start date in September 2027 (or mutually agreed upon). We seek candidates with outstanding research potential or achievement. Successful candidates must have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and contribute to CDM’s education programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Candidates should hold a Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, or a related discipline, and demonstrate a strong research record. Candidates for tenured positions should have an established record of publishing in top-tier journals. We welcome applications from candidates in all areas of finance. In filling one of the two positions, we are particularly interested in candidates working in venture capital, entrepreneurial finance, or private markets. EPFL ranks among the world’s leading universities and offers internationally competitive salaries, generous research support, significant start-up resources, and outstanding research infrastructure. The successful candidates will join an internationally oriented and research-active faculty and will benefit from opportunities for collaboration across EPFL. They will also benefit from EPFL’s partnership with the Swiss Finance Institute (SFI), a private foundation that supports research and teaching in finance in Switzerland. The school provides access to extensive databases, and funding for additional database purchases and computing equipment is readily available. EPFL is located in Lausanne, Switzerland, a beautiful and vibrant city in an Alpine setting on the shores of Lake Geneva, in the heart of Europe. Switzerland offers an exceptionally high standard of living. We offer a highly international environment that is multi-lingual and multi-cultural, and Lausanne is a highly international city. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter including a statement of motivation; curriculum vitae; publication list; research statement; statement of teaching interests; as well as the names and contact of three to five (for the rank of Tenure Track Assistant Professor) or five to seven (for the rank of Associate Professor) references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: November 1, 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/64454656 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Erwan Morellec Director of Swiss Finance Institute @ EPFL Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : searchfinance@epfl.ch Further information on EPFL and CDM is available at epfl.ch and cdm.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-mathematics-of-learning/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning The School of Basic Sciences at EPFL invites applications for a faculty position in Mathematics of Learning . The appointment will be at the Tenure Track level, with an expected start date in fall 2027. We seek outstanding candidates with a research agenda focused on the mathematical foundations of learning and artificial intelligence. Indicative areas include, but are not limited to, theoretical performance guarantees, learning dynamics and generative modelling, sampling and transport methods, statistical foundations, and uncertainty quantification. The candidate should demonstrate the potential to become a leading researcher in their field and is expected to establish an independent, internationally competitive research program. The successful candidate will supervise PhD students, engage with researchers in related fields across the EPFL campus, and show a strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching. EPFL, with its main campus located in Lausanne, Switzerland, on the shores of Lake Geneva, is an international, dynamically growing and well-funded institution fostering excellence and diversity. The EPFL environment is multi-lingual and multi-cultural. As a technical university spanning a broad range of disciplines in engineering and science, EPFL offers an attractive environment for multidisciplinary research collaboration. The mathematical environment at EPFL is strengthened by the Bernoulli Centre for Fundamental Studies, its world-class faculty, and outstanding facilities. Applications should include a cover letter, a CV with a list of publications, a concise statement of research (maximum three pages), a statement of teaching interests (one page), and the names and contact of three to five references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: 1 November, 2026 Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044491 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Maryna Viazovska Director of the Institute of Mathematics Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : [email protected] Further information on EPFL, the School of Basic Sciences, and the Institute of Mathematics is available at epfl.ch , sb.epfl.ch , and math.epfl.ch . EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family-friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open 