    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-theory-and-simulation-of-materials/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials The School of Engineering at EPFL and the Institute of Materials invite applications for a faculty position in Theory and Simulation of Materials . The appointment will be at the Tenure Track Assistant Professor level, with an expected start date in late 2027/early 2028 (or mutually agreed upon). We seek outstanding scientists developing and applying cutting-edge theoretical and computational approaches to understand, predict, and design materials. Areas of particular interest include electronic-structure theory from method development to state-of-the-art, large-scale calculations, multiscale simulations, and data-driven and machine-learning approaches for materials discovery and modeling. A doctorate is required at the starting date. A successful candidate is expected to develop an independent and competitive research program in a multidisciplinary environment. The new Faculty member will supervise their own PhD students and engage with researchers in related fields across the EPFL campus. The successful candidate must have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and contribute to STI education programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The EPFL environment is multilingual and multicultural. EPFL offers internationally competitive salaries, generous research support, significant start-up resources, an outstanding research infrastructure. Academics in Switzerland enjoy many research funding opportunities and an exceptionally high standard of living. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: a cover letter including a brief statement of motivation; a curriculum vitae ; a research statement (max 3 pages) outlining past achievements and future plans; a teaching statement (max 1 page); a full list of scientific outputs , including but not limited to peer-reviewed publications; the names and contact information of three to five referees who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: 1 December 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044493 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Michele Ceriotti Director of the Institute of Materials Chair of the Search Committee Email : [email protected] Further information about EPFL and our Institute is available at: epfl.ch and sti.epfl.ch/imx/ EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and a family-friendly university, committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-tribology-and-interface-engineering-2/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering The School of Engineering at EPFL invites applications for a faculty position in the Institute of Materials (IMX), under the sponsorship of Rolex, in the broad field of tribology, contact mechanics, and surface and interface engineering. The main work location is EPFL’s Neuchâtel campus. The appointment is solicited at the Tenure-Track Assistant Professor level. Exceptional applications may also be considered at the tenured Associate Professor level. Applications are welcome from candidates working across the broad spectrum of research addressing the science and engineering of mutually contacting hard surfaces. Topics of interest include, but are not limited to, the physics, chemistry, mechanics, and microstructural phenomena underlying the performance of materials in friction, wear, adhesion, and lubrication; contact mechanics across length scales; tribocorrosion and environmental degradation of surfaces; protective and functional coatings; and surface and interface engineering of materials for improved tribological performance. Approaches that connect fundamental mechanisms with the design of new materials, surfaces, and solutions for sliding contacts are of particular interest. The successful candidate will develop an independent, internationally recognized research program that complements and strengthens existing activities at EPFL in materials science, mechanics, surface science, and manufacturing. Research that bridges length scales – from atomistic and molecular phenomena at interfaces to the performance of engineered components – and integrates materials design with mechanical behavior is particularly valued. Candidates must hold a PhD and have an outstanding academic record, a compelling research vision, demonstrated scientific impact, and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring students at all levels. A track record in, or clear potential for, technology transfer and collaboration with industry is valued. Application should include: a cover letter including a brief statement of motivation; a curriculum vitae ; a research statement (maximum 3 pages) outlining past achievements as well as future research plans and vision; a teaching statement (maximum 1 page); a full list of scientific outputs , including but not limited to peer-reviewed publications; and the names and contact information of three to five referees who are ready to supply a letter of recommendation upon request. Application deadline: 1 December 2026. Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044496 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Esther Amstad Chair of the Search Committee Email: [email protected] Further information about EPFL and our Institute is available at epfl.ch and sti.epfl.ch/imx/ . EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and a family-friendly university, committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. We strongly encourage women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
    },
    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-energy-systems/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Energy Systems",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Energy Systems ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Energy Systems Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Energy Systems The School of Engineering at EPFL and its Institute of Mechanical Engineering invite applications for a faculty position in Energy Systems . The appointment will be at the Tenure Track level, with an expected start date in Fall 2027 (or a mutually agreed upon date). The main work location is EPFL’s Sion campus. We seek exceptional candidates with expertise in energy systems. The successful candidate will contribute to our mission of developing rigorous and systematic methods for the design, realization, management, operation, and retirement of multi-scale complex systems. The fields of Energy Systems research within Mechanical Engineering include but are not limited to: i) Energy generation and/or conversion, ii) Energy storage, integration and distribution; iii) Energy for extreme environments, such as space; iv) Optimal operations of energy systems. A doctorate is required at the starting date. The candidate is expected to develop an independent and internationally competitive research program in our multidisciplinary environment. The candidate will supervise their PhD students and engage with researchers across EPFL campuses. The successful candidate must have a strong commitment to excellence and innovation in teaching and contribute to Mechanical Engineering education programs at both undergraduate and graduate levels. The EPFL environment is multilingual and multicultural. EPFL offers internationally competitive salaries, generous research support, significant start-up resources, an outstanding research infrastructure, and close ties to the Swiss Federal government as well as to the international policy hub in Geneva. Academics in Switzerland enjoy many research funding opportunities and an exceptionally high standard of living. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter including a statement of motivation; curriculum vitae; publication list; research statement; statement of teaching interests; as well as the names and contact information of three to five references who are willing to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: 01 December 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044497 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Colin Jones Director of the Institute of Mechanical Engineering Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : [email protected] Further information on EPFL, STI and the Institute of Mechanical Engineering are available at: epfl.ch , sti.epfl.ch , valais.epfl.ch and igm.epfl.ch . EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and a family friendly university. We are committed to increasing the diversity of our faculty. We strongly encourage women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
