    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-ethics-of-technology/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology The College of Management of Technology (CDM) at EPFL invites applications for a faculty position in Ethics of Technology, broadly construed. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research examines ethical questions raised by technology, its role in society, and its regulation. The position is open to candidates from a broad range of fields including computer science, cognitive science, economics, engineering, life sciences, statistics and related disciplines. The appointment will be at the Associate or Full Professor level with an expected start date in September 2027 (or mutually agreed upon). The successful candidate will be based in the College of Management of Technology and contribute to its mission of advancing research and education at the interface of technology, organizations, economy, and society. The position is intended to provide intellectual leadership across EPFL on the ethical and societal dimensions of technology. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an ambitious research and teaching program that connects to scientific and technological domains across campus. They must have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and contribute to CDM’s education programs at the undergraduate and graduate levels. EPFL ranks among the world’s leading universities and offers internationally competitive salaries, generous research support, significant start-up resources, and excellent research infrastructure. The successful candidates will join an internationally oriented and research-active faculty and benefit from opportunities for collaboration across EPFL. EPFL is located in Lausanne, Switzerland, a beautiful and vibrant city in an Alpine setting on the shores of Lake Geneva, in the heart of Europe. Switzerland offers an exceptionally high standard of living and Lausanne is a highly international city. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter including a statement of motivation; curriculum vitae; publication list; research statement; statement of teaching interests; as well as the names and contact of five to seven references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: November 15, 2026 . Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65044492 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Daniel Kuhn Director of the Management of Technology & Entrepreneurship institute Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : [email protected] Further information on EPFL and CDM is available at epfl.ch and cdm.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
