    "https://www.epfl.ch/about/working/faculty-position-in-urban-design-and-landscape/": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape",
      "description": "Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape ‒ Working at EPFL ‐ EPFL Skip to content About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Search on the site Validate Show / hide the search form Search on the site Hide the search form EN FR EN DE IT Menu … Afficher l'intégralité du fil d'Ariane About Affiche les pages de même niveau About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus Laboratories list Working at EPFL Affiche les pages de même niveau Organization and identity Associated campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting talent from EPFL Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Contact Faculty Welcome Affiche les pages de même niveau Job opportunities Employment conditions Faculty Welcome Apprenticeships at EPFL Civilian Service Open Faculty Positions Affiche les pages de même niveau Rules and Regulations For Faculty Members Open Faculty Positions Welcome & Onboarding CEAE – EPFL Committee of Academic Evaluation Visiting Professors and Academic Visitors Women Professors Forum Inside Faculty Affairs Contacts Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Affiche les pages de même niveau Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape About Education Research Innovation Schools Campus In the same section Faculty Position in Bioengineering Technologies Faculty Position in Women’s Health Engineering and Digital Technologies Faculty Position in Computational Modeling in Chemistry or Chemical Engineering Faculty Position in Experimental Particle Physics Faculty Positions in Finance Faculty Position in Mathematics of Learning Faculty Position in Theory and Simulation of Materials Faculty Position in Tribology and Interface Engineering Faculty Position in Energy Systems Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences – Security and Privacy Faculty Positions in Computer & Communication Sciences Faculty position in Structural Engineering and Mechanics Faculty Position in Ethics of Technology Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape Faculty Position in Urban Design and Landscape The EPFL School of Architecture, Civil and Environmental Engineering (ENAC) invites applications for an Associate / Full Professor of Urban Design and Landscape in the Institute of Architecture and the City (IA). Urban design sits at the threshold of architecture, territory, landscape architecture and urbanism and focuses on large-scale design of cities and territories. In doing so, urban design requires a transdisciplinary approach that engages architecture, planning, landscape architecture, economics, social sciences and ecology. This holistic approach has become very strategic in the present time, deeply impacted by the climate crisis and social inequality. This present predicament requires a systematic, critical approach that nevertheless should offer tangible visions of ways in which cities and territories can be transformed and made more habitable for humans and non-humans. The successful candidate will be a leading figure in the field, with a solid background in architectural and urban design, and outstanding scientific output, such as books, exhibitions, and papers on the topic. Two aspects are of high importance in the assessment of the candidate. Professional experience in urban projects such as master plans, regulatory planning, and research by design and outstanding track record of teaching experience in both design studio and theory courses. Most importantly, an interest in/or and experience of landscape design will be highly considered, as a clear positioning regarding spatial justice, and a deep awareness of the urgencies connected to the built and unbuilt environment, resource exhaustion, and the social inequalities they bear. For teaching, the new professor will be affiliated with the Section of Architecture and will be expected to teach design studios, offer courses on theoretical and practical aspects of urban design, and supervise both master and doctoral students. Interest in developing innovative and inclusive pedagogies would be of importance. Because of the multidisciplinary and critical character of urban design, the successful candidate will act as a bridge between the different schools of ENAC. Service to the school and involvement in various academic bodies is expected. The successful candidate must have a strong commitment to excellence in teaching. EPFL offers generous research funding and internationally- competitive salaries and benefits. The position will be affiliated with the main campus in Lausanne, on the shores of Lake Geneva. EPFL is a growing and well-funded institution fostering excellence and diversity. It is well equipped with experimental and computational infrastructure and offers a fertile environment for research collaboration between various disciplines. The EPFL environment is multilingual and multicultural. The application package should include the following documents in pdf format: cover letter including a statement of motivation; curriculum vitae; publication list; research statement; statement of teaching interests; as well as the names and contact of five to seven references who are ready to supply a letter upon request. Application deadline: 15.11.2026. Applications should be uploaded to the EPFL recruitment page: https://facultyrecruiting.epfl.ch/position/65863686 Inquiries can be addressed to: Prof. Pier Vittorio Aureli Chair of the Search Committee E-mail : [email protected] Further information on EPFL and ENAC is available at epfl.ch and enac.epfl.ch EPFL is an equal opportunity employer and family friendly university. It is committed to increasing the diversity of its faculty. It strongly encourages women to apply. About Organization and identity Associated Campuses Data Presidency Vice Presidencies Working at EPFL Recruiting EPFL Talents Equality, Diversity, Inclusion Respect Sustainability News & Media Philanthropy EPFL Alumni Education Admission Academic Calendar Preparatory Year (CMS) Bachelor Master Doctorate SHS Program Continuing Education - Extension School Study Management International Teaching Educational Initiatives Education & Science Outreach Infrastructures Under Development Engaging with Society Research Mission and Policy Research Domains EPFL Research Facilities Faculty Members Solutions 4 Sustainability - S4S Awards and Prizes Funding Opportunities Research Management Support From Lab to Market Research Ethics Research with Animals Open Science Innovation Industry Collaboration Innovation Initiatives Startup Launchpad Campus Services & Resources Library Restaurants, Shops & Hotels Security, Prevention & Health Sports Community & Support Chaplaincy Events Arts & Culture Associations Visit EPFL Mobility & Travel Schools & Colleges School of Architecture, Civil & Environmental Engineering ENAC School of Basic Sciences SB School of Engineering STI School of Computer & Communication Sciences IC School of Life Sciences SV College of Management of Technology CDM Practical Services & Resources Emergencies: +41 21 693 3000 Contact Map Follow EPFL on social media Follow us on Facebook Follow us on Instagram Follow us on LinkedIn Follow us on Mastodon Follow us on X Follow us on Youtube Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy policy © 2025 EPFL, all rights reserved Back to top"
